== ProcessSingerPage Template Documentation ==

=== Purpose ===
This template dynamically retrieves specific information from the '''Singer Infobox''' on a queried singer's page using two parameters: the singer's name and the specific field to query.

=== Usage ===
==== Syntax ====
<pre>
{{ProcessSingerPage|<singer_name>|<field>}}
</pre>

==== Parameters ====
* '''singer_name''' (required) – The case-sensitive name of the singer to query from the '''Singer Infobox'''.
* '''field''' (required) – The case-sensitive field name to retrieve from the '''Singer Infobox''' (<nowiki>{{Singer|}}</nowiki>) (e.g., "image", "birthdate", "twitter", etc.).

==== Example ====
<pre>{{ProcessSingerPage|Mafumafu|aka}}</pre>
Output: {{ProcessSingerPage|Mafumafu|aka}}
This will display the specified field (e.g., "aka" for alternative names) from the '''Singer Infobox''' on Mafumafu's page.

===Another Example===
<pre>{{ProcessSingerPage|Amatsuki|officialjapname}}</pre>
Output: {{ProcessSingerPage|Amatsuki|officialjapname}}

=== How It Works ===
The template takes two parameters:
* The first parameter is the singer's name.
* The second parameter is the specific field from the '''Singer Infobox''' you want to query (e.g., image, birthdate, social media links).
* If the field is not found, it will display an error message. If the field exists but has no data, it will display "Unknown".

=== Template Default Return Value ===
If the singer name or the field does not exist, an appropriate error message will be shown.

=== Key Points ===
* The template will retrieve any specified field from the *Singer Infobox Template* <nowiki>{{Singer}}</nowiki> available on the singer's page.
* If the specified field is not found in the '''Singer Infobox''', the template will display an error message.
* You need to provide both the singer's name and the field name for the template to work.

=== Dependencies ===
- This template uses the [[:Module:Singer|Singer Module]] to query the '''Singer Infobox''' and retrieve the specified field for the singer.
